<title>NEW ZEALAND: NBNZ cuts NZ variable mortgage rate to 9.4 pct.</title>
<headline>NBNZ cuts NZ variable mortgage rate to 9.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of New Zealand said on Wednesday it would cut its New Zealand variable home lending rate to 9.4 percent from 9.95 percent.</p>
<p>The move is effective for new business from May 5 and for existing business from May 30.</p>
<p>The bank also said it would cut its one-year fixed home loan rate to 9.25 percent from 9.5 percent, effective for new business from May 5.</p>
<p>Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734746</p>
</text>
